  "title": "Icebound Harbor Builders",
  "rules": [
    "Select any of 512 crew members. Tools can change hands; arrows move one native cell and waiting actors can receive cargo.",
    "Heavy freight moves on foot only beside another actor choosing Anchor that step. Ice takes load stress; roads spend durability under heavy sleds.",
    "A stone builds a nearby wind shelter or ferry landing, otherwise an east-adjacent ice road. Wood fuels shelters; an unbuilt shelter warms nobody.",
    "Quarry, timber and outward freight are finite shared stocks. Deliver freight to a different crew depot for personal and recipient-crew rewards.",
    "A built landing moves a pilot three cells east to actual land and spends local shelter fuel. A rescuer can revive a fallen neighbor with wood.",
    "Sixteen-tick cold exposure reduces health outside heated built shelters. Thirty-two-tick thaw/freeze phases change ice. All actors fallen ends the episode; otherwise stop at 1024."
  ],
